abstract: Qi zheng lue shu (奇症略述) is a Chinese hospital-report publication attributed
  in the Bodleian catalogue to John Glasgow Kerr (J. G. Kerr) and published by 博濟醫局
  (Boji Medical Institution) at Canton (Guangzhou); Sinica 2021 is the 1868 witness.
  Through case narratives and illustrated accounts of patients, it presents the work
  of the Medical Missionary Society’s Hospital at Canton, offering material for studying
  institutional self-presentation, medical charity, case narrative and medical illustration
  in late Qing China. Version 0.2.1 transcribes 31 target physical faces across 19
  images of Bodleian Sinica 2021, providing TXT, JSON and TEI XML with references
  to the official source images. The text is a provisional AI transcription without
  human double collation or expert review. Version 0.2.1 applies only the specified
  non-blind targeted source corrections; it is not a newly completed independent full-book
  second collation.
